 "_exemptRecipes": "Recipes no rule applies to: retired conversions; and, pending a rework of OpV-W's two assembler rows (server_scripts/grindless/opv/wireless.js), the chain strand repeater and the OpV SMES cell, which cannot reach complexFloor 13 (10) at any depth (at most 9.5 and 8.5: three item inputs in a plain assembler); OpV-F2 turned the floor on for the era and held these two by id; the rework (more inputs, fluids, research or another form) deletes both lines. OpV-A4's 37 basic machines (tables/opv_basic_machines.json) are exempt from S-FORM (singles at tier 6 or above in the assembly line): GTM itself makes basic machines in the assembler or at the crafting table, and GTM wins (principle 6); each row already has at least 6 distinct inputs (hull, components, OpV circuits, chain cables, lamina, solder). Singles get no other rule, so the exemption waives S-FORM only; the regex names the 37 machines, not every OpV assembler row.",
 "voltBootstrap": [
  "^gtceu:(uhv|uev|uiv|uxv|opv|max)_energy_(input|output)_hatch_(4|16|64)a$"
 ],
 "_circuitTier": "Concrete circuit items our recipes use and the tier of the #gtceu:circuits/<tier> tag that lists each (native dump dump-uxv-b5m2 tags.json, targeted search); tag inputs (#gtceu:circuits/<tier>) need no entry. voltBootstrap: the multi-amp energy hatches only run at tier N once the tier-N 2 A hatch exists, so like the 2 A hatches they are built at VA[N-1]. ownedPatterns: ids that count as ours without a GTM recipe (gtceu tier components of UHV and above).",
